    "body": "### Problem\n\nnetrw opens in the root dir instead of the current folder.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a9b92dfb-49b2-4771-b49d-9e282f96b718\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nnvim --clean src/test1/test2/test3/test.txt\n`:Explore`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExplore should be inside the src/test1/test2/test3/ folder, not in src/\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-897+g3255e0546f\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nvim -u DEFAULTS doens't have :Explore command, but with vim without flags works fine. so vim src/test1/test2/test3/test.txt + :Explore works fine\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArchLinux - Linux 7.0.10-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.47.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
